+# Outdoor timeline experiments
+
+Private branch: `outdoor-timeline-experiments`, based on `c6671a01`.
+Each new flag requires the exact value `1`; all default off. No launcher changes.
+
+| Target | Flag | Implementation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Upload allocation churn | `KK_UPLOAD_CACHE_EXPANDED=1` | Retain up to 128 returned 128 KiB upload blocks per command pool (16 MiB), versus the existing effective 33. Keep the original return lifecycle and ownership. Requires the rebuilt driver. |
+| Unchanged draw state | `SHADPS4_DYNAMIC_STATE_REUSE=1` | Skip byte-identical repeated setters per deferred command list. Reset on actual graphics pipeline binds, render boundaries and replay. Partial arrays/stencil faces use conservative exact-last-call matching. Direct mode stays unconditional. |
+| Fault/tracker bookkeeping | `SHADPS4_RANGE_PROTECTION=1` | Compute CPU-write protection differences within the affected page range. Preserve watcher callbacks and ordering. GPU/read protection keeps the full-region path. Remove no faults, waits, uploads or GPU-generation checks. |
+| Compute attribution | `SHADPS4_COMPUTE_DISPATCH_LABELS=1` | Balanced debug groups for guest direct/indirect compute and host tiling/detiling. Include shader hash, group/local sizes, or layout/bit depth/mips/slices. No waits, timestamps or forced encoder boundaries. |
+
+`KK_UPLOAD_CACHE_DIAGNOSTICS=1` prints created/reused/destroyed block counters at pool destruction. Counters are independent of the larger cache flag. Free-block accounting is initialized on creation and reset on trim/destruction.
+
+Compute attribution is instrumentation, not a proven kernel optimization. The previous trace did not identify a specific hot kernel. Native Metal capture/debug groups provide the next evidence. Indirect group counts are unknown (shown as zero), without reading guest/GPU memory. Driver-generated graphics-emulation kernels are outside guest compute groups; distinguish them using existing pipeline/kernel names. Debug-utils absence disables labels safely. Keep labels and counters off during FPS measurements. No old HLE/single-mip experiments are enabled.
+
+## Validation
+
+All four implementations and their tests were written before starting builds/tests. Focused tests exercise the real recorder through fake Vulkan dispatch, actual region tracking through captured watcher callbacks, randomized range-mask equivalence and upload policy limits. Policy tests do not establish GPU completion safety or gameplay correctness.
+
+From the engine root (separate architecture build directories):
+
+```sh
+cmake -S tests/outdoor_experiments -B /private/tmp/guardian-outdoor-unit-arm64 -G Ninja -DCMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES=arm64
+cmake --build /private/tmp/guardian-outdoor-unit-arm64 -j 6
+ctest --test-dir /private/tmp/guardian-outdoor-unit-arm64 --output-on-failure
+cmake -S tests/outdoor_experiments -B /private/tmp/guardian-outdoor-unit-x86_64 -G Ninja -DCMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES=x86_64
+cmake --build /private/tmp/guardian-outdoor-unit-x86_64 -j 6
+ctest --test-dir /private/tmp/guardian-outdoor-unit-x86_64 --output-on-failure
+cmake --build build-macos --target shadps4 -j 6
+```
+
+Assertions remain active in the focused suite. Preserve the copied outdoor save, guarded runner, SOTC exclusion and owned-process cleanup for native trials. Test independently before combining. Retain 720p, effects, precise readbacks, VBlank 120 and the installed four combined flags. Validate outdoor/pool rendering, Trico/feather behavior, movement, transitions and save/reload before promotion.
+
+Results, patches and hashes: `logs/outdoor-four-experiments-20261017/` (in the maintainer's workspace).
